course: dictionary
lesson: 13500
title: Words that mean perfect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have a strong meaning, and the words around them show you what it is. «Her bedroom was immaculate: the bed was made and not a sock was on the floor.» The clues are a made bed and no socks on the floor, so immaculate must mean spotless and tidy.
explain: Immaculate can also mean perfect, with no mistakes. «The band gave an immaculate performance, and not one note was wrong.» Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: perfect performance still makes sense.
explain: The adverb is immaculately, which tells you how something is done. «He was immaculately dressed for the wedding» means his clothes were perfectly neat. When you meet a new word, ask what it describes, then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Immaculate means perfectly clean and tidy, with no dirt or mess at all.
fact: Immaculate can also mean without any mistake, perfect.
fact: «Immaculately» is the adverb: «She was immaculately dressed.»
fact: Phrases to remember are «in immaculate condition» and «immaculate handwriting».
fact: In church teaching, the «Immaculate Conception» is a Catholic belief that Mary was free of original sin from the start of her life. It is celebrated on 8 December.
exercise: «Her bedroom was immaculate: the bed was made and not a sock was on the floor.» What does immaculate mean? | *Perfectly clean and tidy | Messy and full of toys | Very dark and quiet | Broken
exercise: «The band gave an immaculate performance.» What does immaculate suggest here? | Too short | *No mistakes at all | Late | Funny and loud
exercise: «The old car was in immaculate condition, with no scratches or dents.» Which clues show what immaculate means? | Parked on a steep hill | A very noisy engine | Lots of rain on the windows | *No scratches or dents
test: «She wrote her name in immaculate handwriting.» What does immaculate mean? | *Neat and perfect, with no mistakes | Written in pencil | Hard to read | Very large
test: «He was immaculately dressed for the wedding.» What does immaculately mean? | Very sadly | Without any shoes | *In a perfectly neat way | In a rushed and messy way
exam: Which is the best meaning of immaculate in «an immaculate white shirt»? | *Spotless and perfectly clean | Too big | Torn and dirty | Bright red
